<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves down at $1.567 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves down at $1.567 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves were down at $1.567 billion on April 26 from $1.588 billion a week before and against $2.255 billion on April 25, 1996, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Friday.</p>
<p>Pakistan's weekly foreign exchange reserves holdings position:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		APRIL 26   APRIL 19   APRIL 25, 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL</p>
<p>				  1,567	1,588	2,255</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan	   691	  600	  1,265</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan    191	  310	  281</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion    674	  676	  697</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights    11	   2	    12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
